==Trivia==
*In the comics, Cassandra Nova is the twin sister of [[Charles Xavier]] who was nearly killed while in the womb. A fierce enemy of the [[X-Men]], she is most famous for orchestrating the genocide on Genosha, killing more than fifteen million mutant residents with a rogue [[Sentinels|Sentinel]].
*She is the fifth female main antagonist in a [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] film, following [[Hela]], [[Ghost]], [[Scarlet Witch]] and [[Dar-Benn]].
*Nova is the fourth main antagonist to be killed by the titular character(s) of the film in which she appears.
*Cassandra Nova is the second main antagonist of an Marvel Cinematic Universe film to originate from another universe, the first being [[Green Goblin]].

==Behind the Scenes== 
*[[Emma Corrin]]'s casting as Cassandra Nova was because ''[[Deadpool & Wolverine]]'' director [[Shawn Levy]] saw them in a performance of {{WPS|Virginia Woolf}}'s ''{{WPS|Orlando: A Biography}}'' stage play in 2022, with Corrin accepting the role as they were interested in playing a villain.<ref>[https://www.empireonline.com/movies/news/emma-corrin-villain-deadpool-3/ Emma Corrin On The OA Creators’ New Show A Murder At The End Of The World: ‘It’s So Ahead Of Its Time’]</ref>
*[[Marvel Studios]] eyed Emma Corrin to play Cassandra Nova since late 2022 around {{WPS|Christmas}}, but they had to work out their busy schedule to make sure they could fully commit to the role, settling any arrangements around early February 2023.<ref>[https://deadline.com/2023/02/deadpool-3-emma-corrin-lands-lead-role-in-marvel-studios-sequel-1235258306/ ‘Deadpool 3’: Emma Corrin Lands Lead Role In Marvel Studios Sequel]</ref>
*''[[Deadpool & Wolverine]]'' casting director [[Sarah Halley Finn]] cast Emma Corrin as Cassandra Nova due to feeling they could hold their own opposite [[Ryan Reynolds (actor)|Ryan Reynolds]] and [[Hugh Jackman]], feeling that Nova had to encompass her power in a unique and fresh way, resulting in Finn loving how Corrin played the role.<ref>[https://variety.com/2025/artisans/news/jonathan-bailey-almost-missed-wicked-1236295150/ Casting Directors Reveal How Jonathan Bailey Almost Missed Out on ‘Wicked’ and Why Emma Corrin Made the Perfect ‘Deadpool & Wolverine’ Villain]</ref>
*Emma Corrin was praised by Ryan Reynolds and Hugh Jackman for being like "a skin-covered {{WPS|Swiss Army knife}}" to work with and their ability to "subtly change - to turn on a dime" with an effortlessness while portraying Cassandra Nova, with Reynolds feeling that Corrin brought a {{WPS|Gene Wilder}}-type of energy to Nova, made her motivations easier to understand and humanized her dialogue by inspiring themselves on {{WPS|Christopher Waltz}}'s {{WPS|Hans Landa}} from ''{{WPS|Inglourious Basterds}}''.<ref>[https://www.harpersbazaar.com/culture/film-tv/a60814103/emma-corrin-interview-june-july-2024/ Emma Corrin Is in a League of Their Own]</ref>
*To help inform their own performance as Cassandra Nova, Emma Corrin looked back at the performances of both [[Patrick Stewart]] and {{WPS|James McAvoy}} as {{WPS|Charles Xavier (film character)|Charles Xavier/Professor X}} in {{WPS|20th Century Studios|20th Century Fox}}'s {{WPS|X-Men (film series)|''X-Men'' film series}} with some reluctance to not resemble their performances too close. They ultimately opted to look for any bits they could pay homage to for fans to enjoy and to faithfully adapt Nova from the source material in both looks and origins.<ref>[https://screenrant.com/deadpool-wolverine-cassandra-nova-xmen-professor-x-connection-emma-corrin-response/ Deadpool & Wolverine: Cassandra Nova's Family History With Professor X & More X-Men Connections Teased By Star]</ref>

